From 60ce612abd173adec985c61efb4de2e629225ed7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:59:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] upstream sync gate: require an independent
 exact-head review for a fork-authored sync

Core PR #2479 (upstream sync 254119c6f5) landed through scripts/ci/upstream_sync.py with
no review, although it carried fork-authored code: 17 remerge-diff files (conflict
resolutions and fork edits) plus a test fixup. The fork's rule for code is an independent
exact-head approval plus green required CI.

The gate now classifies a sync head before landing it (scripts/ci/upstream_sync_review.py):
- mechanical: every merge it brings that upstream/main lacks has an empty
  `git show --remerge-diff`, and it brings no other commit. These land exactly as before.
- fork-authored: anything else. It lists the resolution files per merge and the fork
  commits. It merges only after hermes-core-wt ship's own review gate approves the PR's
  exact head: keyed_review_card / request_review files the review card, review_gate
  reads the verdict, review_reply_guard holds unanswered non-blocking points. Until
  then the gate prints NOT YET naming the review card (or, in a worker shell, the exact
  kanban_create to file). A host without the ship tool, or with a tool that lacks those
  entry points, refuses instead of landing.

`upstream_sync.py --classify REV [--base REV]` is the dry run: it prints the verdict and
lands nothing (for a landed head it classifies against main just before it landed).
--review-reply and --impl-task pass through to ship's gate. The landing PR body names
the fork-authored content a reviewer should read. .github/LANDING.md says which syncs
need review.

Tests (tests/scripts/ci/test_upstream_sync_review.py, real bare remotes, ship's module
stubbed through HERMES_CORE_WT_LAND): conflict-resolution sync parks then lands on an
exact-head approval; a mechanical sync lands with no review; a [daveey] fixup with no
conflict parks; an unreadable or drifted ship tool refuses; worker review-card action;
unanswered points park; classify dry run. Mutants on the classifier (drop the
remerge-diff check, drop the fixup check, invert the verdict) each fail named tests.

